{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Rule-based, Publish-subscribe and Peer to Peer Architecture Styles"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about rule-based, publish-subscribe and peer to peer architecture styles."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the application installation program, using IT development tools available in the market, based on solution architecture features.  Recognizes and implements the different types of architecture styles that can be included in the IT solution"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Exchanges simple information on the hardware devices and the architecture of a system to create the IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<strong>What to + verb.</strong>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use <strong>what to + verb </strong>to give emphasis to an object or thing before the verb.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Subscribers decide what to view since the publishers don't send the messages directly and they can filter the information by tittle or content."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Unfortunately publishers don't know exactly what to post since they need to know the subscribers' interests."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You tell the system what to interpret and it analyzes the axioms in order to give logic answers to problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>What </strong>refers to an object or a thing, it helps us provide a content to a sentence depending on the action.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Let&rsquo;s review these sentences:</p> <ul> <li><span class=\"italic\">Publishers only care about <span class=\"strong\">what they post</span>.&nbsp;</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Publisher only care about <strong>what to post.</strong></span></li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the previous sentence we can see how the verb <strong>post </strong>gives meaning to <strong>what. </strong>Now, instead of repeating the subject we can give the same meaning to the sentence by using <strong>what to.</strong>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<strong>Rule-based, publish-subscribe and peer to peer architecture styles.</strong>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "These architecture styles are commonly used for problem solving, sharing data, and obtaining data. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Rule-based</strong> has to do with ways to manage data, usually manipulated by artificial intelligence applications.</p> <p><strong>Publish-subscribe </strong>refers to senders of messages called publishers and receivers called subscribers.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> <p><strong>Peer-to-peer</strong> is a method to distribute services between peers that work as consumers and servers at the same time.&nbsp;</p> <p>In the following chart, we will see some characteristics of each type. </p>"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10img01.jpg"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This system uses a semantic reasoner that matches the information, establishes a conflict-resolution process, and acts accordingly."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Publish-subscribe pattern is about data sent by publishers and obtained by subscribers."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's a network where all peers are designed to be suppliers and consumers of services."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "semantic reasoner"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "software that infers logical consequences from facts  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This system uses a semantic reasoner that matches the information, establishes a conflict-resolution process, and acts accordingly. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "axiom "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "statements that a system considers true by logic"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You tell the system what to interpret and it analyzes the axioms in order to give logic answers to problems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "compiler "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "program that converts code language into programming language"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Rule-based system are used as compilers to interpret computer programs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "infer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to interpret a message by using logics"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Basically the reasoner infers information and takes action based on the input that it has."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "peer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something or someone with the same characteristics"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peers communicate by nodes and the type of connection depends on the network."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "subscriber "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "receiver of messages provided by a publisher"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Subscribers decide what to view since the publishers don't send the messages directly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about rule-based, peer to peer and publish-subscribe architecture style. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes about the information of each architecture style. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a description with your own words about each architecture style."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a brochure with your description to promote each architecture style."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your brochure with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about rule-based, peer to peer and publish-subscribe architecture style.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a description of each architecture style."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share with my partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Sonia:</strong> What is your favorite app to listen to music?<br /><strong>Leonard: </strong>&nbsp;I know Spotify\u00ae is considered more popular but I prefer Napster\u00ae. Anyway they follow similar peer-to-peer principles.<br /><strong>Sonia:</strong> What do you mean?<br /><strong>Leonard: </strong>&nbsp;Let me describe to you what peer-to-peer is and what to take into account. It&rsquo;s a network where all peers are designed to be suppliers and consumers of services. Peers communicate by nodes and the type of connection depends on the network, if it&rsquo;s structured, the system organizes the protocol to ensure that files are found easily. If the network is unstructured, there are random connections among peers. These styles are used in public-sharing apps such as Napster\u00ae. Spotify\u00ae uses a hybrid model, though.<br /><strong>Sonia:</strong> I thought that the architecture style they used was called publish-subscribe."}, {"time": "46500", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Leonard: </strong>&nbsp;Not really. Publish-subscribe pattern is about data sent by publishers and obtained by subscribers. Subscribers decide what to view since the publishers don&rsquo;t send the messages directly and they can filter the information by tittle or content. Unfortunately, publishers don&rsquo;t know exactly what to post since they need to know the subscribers&rsquo; interests. One big advantage of this style is the scalability that it can reach. It is commonly used for databases or mailing lists.<br /><strong>Sonia:</strong> I see, that&rsquo;s the same style that expert systems uses!"}, {"time": "78700", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Leonard: </strong>&nbsp;Actually, no! They use a rule-based system. You tell the system what to interpret and it analyzes the axioms in order to give logic answers to problems. This system uses a semantic reasoner that matches the information, establishes a conflict-resolution process, and acts accordingly. Basically, the reasoner infers information and takes action based on the input that it has. Rule-based system are used as compilers to interpret computer programs.<br /><strong>Sonia:</strong> I forgot you were an expert in architecture styles!"}